<title>GUATEMALA: Guatemala exports 438,042 T sugar to March 11.</title>
<headline>Guatemala exports 438,042 T sugar to March 11.</headline>
<dateline>GUATEMALA CITY 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Guatemala has exported 438,042 tonnes of sugar since Nov. 1, the Central American Isthmus Sugar Producers said Tuesday in an update.</p>
<p>The export report covers the period of Guatemala's current 1996-1997 sugar harvest up through March 11.</p>
<p>According to the report, the United States was the major destination of Guatemalan sugar exports. Under the quota system, 59,015 tonnes of raw sugar have been exported to the United States.</p>
<p>Guatemala imported and re-exported an additional 134,933 tonnes of raw sugar to the United States, it added.</p>
<p>Of the total amount exported to date, refined sugar exports were 129,694 tonnes and raws were 308,348 tonnes.</p>
<p>Other destinations include 77,400 tonnes to Chile (all refined), 50,000 to Morocco (all raws), 41,700 to Sri Lanka (27,700 refined, 14,000 raws), 36,000 to Mexico (all raws), and smaller amounts to the Ivory Coast, Haiti, Jamaica and Peru.</p>
<p>((--Fiona Ortiz, Guatemala City bureau +502 251-5718))</p>
